WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
Picture a model that aces a Python quiz but can still fall apart renaming a function used across forty files.

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.660
That's why I'd compare the best LLMs for coding on SWE-bench Verified,

3
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:15.033
where a model has to resolve an actual GitHub issue.

4
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:18.493
Claude 4.6 Opus leads that benchmark,

5
00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:21.733
but the right model still depends on the kind of work.

6
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:25.793
For an unattended agent on multi-file pull requests I'd reach for Claude,

7
00:00:25.793 --> 00:00:28.333
and to reason over a whole repository,

8
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:30.367
Gemini 3.1 Pro.

9
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:33.227
So rather than one model for everything,

10
00:00:33.347 --> 00:00:36.247
I'd route autocomplete to a small fast model.
